./docs/articles/new-expensify/bank-accounts/Connect-a-Bank-Account.md:74:# How to delete a verified bank account
./docs/articles/new-expensify/bank-accounts/Connect-a-Bank-Account.md:75:If you need to delete a bank account from Expensify, run through the following steps:
./docs/articles/new-expensify/billing-and-plan-types/The-Free-Plan.md:57:- You can edit or delete any expense that hasn’t been paid or closed by your admin.
./docs/articles/new-expensify/billing-and-plan-types/The-Free-Plan.md:135:Users can edit and delete expenses on Processing reports. If you need something changed, let them know by commenting in the Report History section of the report on expensify.com or by chatting with them in new.expensify.com.
./docs/articles/new-expensify/billing-and-plan-types/The-Free-Plan.md:145:## As an admin, can I edit users’ expenses and delete them from reports?
./docs/articles/new-expensify/billing-and-plan-types/The-Free-Plan.md:147:No. Only users can edit and delete expenses on the Free plan. Admin control of submitted expenses on a workspace is a feature of our paid plans. If you need something changed, let the user know by commenting in the Report History section of the report on www.expensify.com or by chatting with them in new.expensify.com.
./docs/articles/new-expensify/chat/Introducing-Expensify-Chat.md:101:If you mouse-over a message (or long-press on mobile), you will see the action menu. This allows you to add a reaction, start a thread, copy the link, mark it as unread, edit your own message, delete your own message, or flag it as offensive.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/integrations/accounting-integrations/NetSuite.md:221:If you want to delete Categories, you must do this in NetSuite. Categories are added and modified on the integration’s side and then synced with Expensify.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/integrations/accounting-integrations/NetSuite.md:230:If you want to delete Tags, you must do this in NetSuite. Tags are added and modified on the integration’s side and then synced with Expensify.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/integrations/travel-integrations/Additional-Travel-Integrations.md:63:A: Automatic mode is less effort as it’s easier to delete an expense in Expensify than to remember to forward a forgotten receipt.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/getting-started/Tips-And-Tricks.md:48:5. Check the “Not allowed to see your location” list to ensure that expensify.com and new.expensify.com are not listed. If they are, click the delete icon next to them to allow location access
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/account-settings/Close-Account.md:23:Look for the "Close Account" option in the "Others" section. (If you don’t see this option, you have a Domain Controlled account and will need to ask your Domain Admin to delete your account.)
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/account-settings/Close-Account.md:58:1. If you're part of a group workspace, request the Workspace Admin to remove you, or if you own the workspace, delete it to downgrade to a free version.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/account-settings/Close-Account.md:73:- **Account Under a Validated Domain**: If your account is associated with a validated domain, only a Domain Admin can close it. You can find this option in your Domain Admin's settings under Settings > Domains > Domain Members. Afterward, if you have a secondary personal login, you can delete it by following the instructions mentioned above.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/account-settings/Account-Details.md:41:3. You can keep the old address as a secondary login or delete email addresses by selecting the **"Remove"** button.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/get-paid-back/reports/Create-A-Report.md:118:# How to delete a report
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/get-paid-back/reports/Create-A-Report.md:122:Click Details in the top-right of the report on the web app, then click the Trash icon to delete the report. Any expenses on the report will move to an Unreported state.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/get-paid-back/reports/Create-A-Report.md:126:To delete a Draft report on an Android, press and hold the report name and tap **Delete**.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/get-paid-back/reports/Create-A-Report.md:128:To delete a Draft report on an iOS device, go to the **Reports** screen, swipe the report to the left, and tap **Delete**.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/get-paid-back/reports/Create-A-Report.md:132:If you want to delete a Processing or Closed report, please follow the How to undo your report submission instructions in this article to move the report back into an Draft status, then follow the steps above.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/get-paid-back/reports/Create-A-Report.md:134:If you want to delete an Approved or Reimbursed report, please speak to your Company Admin as this may not be possible.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/get-paid-back/Per-Diem-Expenses.md:35:Per Diems cannot be amended. To make changes, delete the expense and recreate it as needed.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/manage-employees-and-report-approvals/Removing-Members.md:6:Removing a member from a workspace disables their ability to use the workspace. Please note that it does not delete their account or deactivate the Expensify Card.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/manage-employees-and-report-approvals/Removing-Members.md:36:If you have a Control Workspace and have Domain Control enabled, you will need to remove them from the domain to delete members' accounts entirely and deactivate the Expensify Card.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/workspace-and-domain-settings/Invoicing.md:64:If you want to delete a report field, click the red trashcan on the field in your **Workspace** > **Individual** or **Group** > **Report** settings to remove it from all future invoices. Unsent invoices will have a red **X** next to the report field, which you can click to remove before sending the invoice to your customer.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/workspace-and-domain-settings/Categories.md:58:4. Add new categories by tapping the **+** button in the upper right corner. To delete a category, on iOS swipe left, on Android press and hold. Tap a category name to edit it.
